# Task 9 Report — Focused Final Verification and Canary Readiness Handoff

## Status

Blocked at the prescribed focused test gates. Both compile commands passed, but each one-shot pytest suite reported Windows permission failures in test-created audit/controller temporary paths. The suites were not rerun. Because the architecture gate remained red, the final two-fold parity, manifest build, emitted prepare command, readiness inspection, and canary handoff generation were not launched.

The implementation worktree remained on `codex/pit-optimizer-implementation` at a committed HEAD with no tracked or untracked status entry before verification. All sealed local input paths existed with the expected file or directory type; both JSON inputs parsed, and the PIT bundle had the SQLite file signature. The two create-only Task 9 outputs were absent at preflight.

## Compile evidence

The prescribed compile commands were each run exactly once:

- `compileall`: exit 0 with no output; 13 Python sources were in scope (7 under `core/strategy_policy` plus 6 explicitly named production modules).
- `py_compile`: exit 0 with no output; 4 explicitly named production modules were in scope.

Total compile scope: 17 Python source files across two successful commands.

## Test evidence

The focused architecture suite was run exactly once:

